371106","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112473#issuecomment-3501371106","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112473","id":3501371106,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Qsq7i","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T08:58:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T08:58:13Z","body":"There's a more readable message, but it's only enabled in debug builds:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cb3af5afff15669a684ba4f04b9aa5c70dfd09ad/drivers/windows/file_access_windows.cpp#L102-L106\n\n> Attempting to create a file named 'com1' with any extension, anywhere in the FileSystem docker will fail. If you externally create or manually rename a file to com1, the engine will fail to open it.\n\nBehavior itself is expected, you should not use reserved names, including reserved name with any extension, Windows can handle these, but documentation say to avoid using it - [Naming Files, Paths, and Namespaces](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/naming-a-file#naming-conventions)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https: